From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Eleven more live switches: list fetch, DMA clear, semaphore reads, caches

DRAFT, not built. With EDEN_UP_LIVE_SWITCHES=1 these can change while the game runs
(common/live_switch.h). Without it each is what env.txt gave at its first use, for ever, with its
own parsing rules, and the cost where it is off stays one read where there was one.

Armed (they only change anything when on in env.txt at boot, because something they rely on is
set up or kept only then; off at boot, a phase that turns them on does nothing and the app says so):
- EDEN_UP_L1056_LIST_FETCH: the front's wait before a command list entry. #1056's target
  (synced_writer_position) is only noted when a rule was on at boot. Read once per entry
  (dma_pusher.cpp ListFetchRuleNow) for its wait, its second look and its check together; off,
  the entry takes the rule it has without the switch (#1055 if set, else LISTSYNC's or the wait
  for every writer), which waits for the same work or more. No per-list state is kept or shared
  with the back.
- EDEN_NX2_SEM_FAST (0/1/2): the front's write notes (FrontMemoryNotesEnabled) are boot-only.
  Read at each acquire, poll and SEM_EXECUTE; 0 takes the drained path. The delayed-fence and
  split checks in SemaphoreReadableNow are unchanged.
- EDEN_PE_IMAGE_PAGES: the texture cache's page marks (RegisterImage) stay boot-only; each guest
  read (GetFlushArea) reads the switch once.
- EDEN_PE_NO_EMPTY_SUBMITS: FlushWork's tick note stays boot-only; each fence flush reads it.
- EDEN_NX2_PIPELINE_CLEAN: a plain lookup forgets the clean lookup's answer (clean.pipeline) in a
  run with the switch on at boot, so the first clean lookup after an off phase takes a new
  snapshot. Peek per lookup, first use in the PipelineCache constructor.
- EDEN_NX2_INVALIDATION_FILTER: the filters are made and marked only when on at boot.
  PageFilter::Any reads it (Peek, first use in the PageFilter constructor) after its own
  "no filter" check, so a run with it off at boot reads nothing new.

Live:
- EDEN_UP_L1094_DMACLEAR: per DMA clear. A clear the quarter check missed in an off phase leaves
  that buffer's old words until it is written again, as in a run without the switch.
- EDEN_UP_DRAIN_SKIP_SAME: per semaphore word read. Off reads note nothing; the noted words only
  claim "nothing was sent since", which write_position checks. EDEN_NX2_READBACK_WAIT still turns
  it off for good.
- EDEN_UP_OOT_POLL_BACKOFF_US (a number, us): per SVC. Needs EDEN_UP_OOT_POLL_BACKOFF=1 at boot.
  ParsePollBackoffUs keeps the old rules: above 1, at most 16000, else 4000.
- EDEN_NX2_TABLES_SPEED: per upload scan; the upload epoch counts for every value.
- EDEN_NX2_RANGE_PREFIX: per range lookup; every entry is a full walk of its own range.

All but L1056_LIST_FETCH, L1094_DMACLEAR and OOT_POLL_BACKOFF_US are in TranslationSwitches
(vk_pipeline_prep.cpp, left alone): set in env.txt they pick another prepared-shader store. A
live plan leaves the plain live ones out of env.txt and sets them in the schedule; the armed ones
must be in env.txt, so such a plan boots with their store.

Not made live here: EDEN_GBB_PIPELINE_ONCE (the PS5 build's prepare-vulkan-port.py already hands
UpdateDynamicStates the prepared pipeline, so the switch changes nothing there), EDEN_NX2_CB_BATCH
and EDEN_NX2_INDEX_REBIND (first look only).

Anchors of prepare-vulkan-port.py (adapt blocks, the _cost.cpp generators, shader_costs) and the
maxwell_3d.cpp line macro_native.cmake rewrites counted on T121 before and after: unchanged.

